Well, there is a problem: 

it don't work like that in regular game play!  You can wish for a wand of
wishing (or magic lantern), and get one, but they *always* have no charges
left *and are not rechargeable*.  I know with wands, you can squeeze one
more charge out of them (and then they explode), but that only gets you back
the wish you used to get the wand...  The Dev Team was way ahead of you.

If there are any infinite-wish scams existing in NetHack, they are a pretty
damn well-kept secret.

Given a single wish wand, the most you can get seems to be:
x ( - 1 ) + 3 + 1

where x is the initial number of charges in the wand (1-3), maybe -1 wish to 
get some blessed scrolls of charging, +3 for the number of wishes after the 
recharge, and 1 final wish you can wrest out of the wand.  You can only
recharge a wand or lamp once (it explodes upon second recharge).

